---
import Article from '../components/Article.astro';
const home = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Article title="">
  <p class="intro">Thank you for your interest!</p>
  <p>Drop your email in the form below and we'll be in touch</p>

  <form class="signup-form" aria-describedby="signup-status signup-purpose">
    <p id="signup-status" class="signup-status">
      Registration opens soon.
    </p>
    <fieldset disabled>
      <legend class="sr-only">Register interest in RoadSpace</legend>
      <label for="signup-email">Email address</label>
      <input id="signup-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required />
      <label class="consent" for="signup-consent">
        <input id="signup-consent" name="consent" type="checkbox" required />
        <span>
          I agree to ROADSPACE LLC using my information in accordance with the{' '}
          <a href="#privacy">Privacy Notice</a> below.
        </span>
      </label>
      <button class="button" type="submit">
        Register <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </button>
    </fieldset>
    <p id="signup-purpose" class="form-note">
      You can withdraw your registration and/or have your personal information deleted by emailing
      [PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL].
    </p>
  </form>

  <section id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Privacy Notice</h2>
    <p class="notice-date">Effective date: [DATE]</p>

    <h3>Who we are</h3>
    <p>
      RoadSpace is operated by ROADSPACE LLC, based in Connecticut, USA. For requests concerning
      your personal information, including withdrawal of your registration or deletion of your data,
      email [PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL].
    </p>

    <h3>What we collect and why</h3>
    <p>
      When you register, we collect your email address, registration date, and a record of your
      consent. We use this information to maintain your registration, prevent duplicate records,
      measure interest, and respond to requests concerning your information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Registration is voluntary. We do not subscribe you to a newsletter or send promotional emails
      as part of this registration.
    </p>
    <p>
      [figure out exact terms of rollout phases, how you'll send out download links, how long
      they'll be good for, who gets them, etc; people should expect be contacted regarding their
      participation, but you want to make sure it's clear you're not going to be annoying]
    </p>

    <h3>Technical information</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting and security providers, GitHub and Cloudflare, process technical information such
      as IP addresses and request information to deliver and protect the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      [DESCRIBE ANY APPLICATION LOGS, IP RETENTION, COOKIES, ANALYTICS, OR BOT-PROTECTION TOOLS
      ACTUALLY USED, INCLUDING THEIR PURPOSES AND RETENTION.]
    </p>

    <h3>Who receives information</h3>
    <p>
      Cloudflare provides the infrastructure that processes and stores registrations on our behalf.
      Access within RoadSpace is limited to people who need it to operate the registration service.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell your registration information or use it for targeted advertising. We may
      disclose information where legally required.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may publish aggregate registration counts. We do not publish email addresses or individual
      registration records.
    </p>

    <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
    <p>
      We retain your registration for [RETENTION PERIOD] after signup, unless you withdraw sooner.
      We then delete it or remove identifying information. Backup copies expire according to [BACKUP
      RETENTION PERIOD].
    </p>

    <h3>Your choices and requests</h3>
    <p>
      To withdraw your registration, request deletion, correct your address, or request a copy of
      your registration information, email [PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL], preferably from the registered
      address. We may take reasonable steps to verify your request.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where processing relies on your consent, you may withdraw it at any time. Withdrawal does not
      affect the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on applicable law, you may have additional rights, including the right to complain
      to your local data-protection authority.
    </p>

    <h3>International processing</h3>
    <p>
      Our providers may process information outside your state or country. [CONFIRM PROCESSING
      LOCATIONS AND DESCRIBE APPLICABLE INTERNATIONAL-TRANSFER SAFEGUARDS WHERE REQUIRED.]
    </p>
  </section>
  <p class="back-link">
    <a href={home}>&larr; Back to RoadSpace</a>
  </p>
</Article>

<style>
  .signup-form {
    margin: 1rem 0 3rem;
    padding: 1.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  fieldset {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  input[type='email'] {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1.4rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: #202020;
    color: var(--foreground);
    font: inherit;
  }
  .consent {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }
  .consent input {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .button {
    font-family: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .button:disabled {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .signup-status {
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }
  .form-note,
  .notice-date {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }
  #privacy {
    padding-top: 1.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
  }
  #privacy p {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  .back-link {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
